    "answer": {
      "short": "$1+\\sqrt[4]2+\\sqrt2+\\sqrt[4]8$.\n\nUse the difference of squares twice.",
      "worked": "Let $t=\\sqrt[4]2$, so $t^4=2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac1{t-1}&=\\frac{t+1}{t^2-1}\\\\\\frac1{t-1}&=\\frac{(t+1)(t^2+1)}{t^4-1}\\\\\\frac1{t-1}&=t^3+t^2+t+1.\\end{align*}$$\nHence\n$$\\frac1{\\sqrt[4]2-1}=1+\\sqrt[4]2+\\sqrt2+\\sqrt[4]8.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
